    {
      "text": "CONSTRUCTION OF IRREDUCIBLE REPRESENTATIONS OVER KHOVANOV-LAUDA-ROUQUIER ALGEBRAS — We give an explicit construction of irreducible modules over Khovanov-Lauda- Rouquier algebras R and their\n\n**CONSTRUCTION OF IRREDUCIBLE REPRESENTATIONS OVER KHOVANOV-LAUDA-ROUQUIER ALGEBRAS**\n\n*OF FINITE CLASSICAL TYPE*\n\n45 pp, 10 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** We give an explicit construction of irreducible modules over Khovanov-Lauda- Rouquier algebras R and their cyclotomic quotients Rλ for ﬁnite classical types using a crystal basis theoretic approach. More precisely, for each element v of the crystal B(∞) (resp. B(λ)), we ﬁrst construct certain modules ∆(a; k) labeled by the adapted string a of v. We then prove that the head of the induced module Ind \u0000∆(a; 1)⊠· · ·⊠∆(a; n) \u0001 is irreducible and that every irreducible R-module (resp. Rλ-module) can be realized as the irreducible head of one of the induced modules Ind(∆(a; 1) ⊠· · · ⊠∆(a; n)). Moreover, we show that our construction is compatible with the crystal structure on B(∞) (resp. B(λ)).\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; Introduction; 1.1 Crystals; 1 Crystals and Khovanov-Lauda-Rouquier Algebra; 1.2 Khovanov-Lauda-Rouquier algebras; 1.3 Construction of irreducible R-modules; 2 Description of Nk(v) for Finite Type Via Ada; 3 Explicit Construction of Irreducible Modules; 4 Proof of Theorem ??; References",
